the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a person* is a rival of *a other person*.
*a person* has a different favourite than *a other person*.
*a person* likes *a thing*.
*a person* favourite is *a thing*.

the knowledge base rivalry includes:

a person is a rival of a other person
    if the person likes a thing
    and the other person likes the thing
    and the person is not equal to the other person.

a person has a different favourite than a other person
    if the person favourite is a thing
    and the other person favourite is a other thing
    and the thing is different from the other thing.

scenario one is:
    Alice likes chess.
    Bob likes chess.
    Alice favourite is tea.
    Bob favourite is coffee.
    one expects answers ["Alice is a rival of Bob", "Bob is a rival of Alice"].
    two expects answers ["Alice has a different favourite than Bob", "Bob has a different favourite than Alice"].

query one is:
    which person is a rival of which other person.

query two is:
    which person has a different favourite than which other person.
